 * NOT measured: precision/recall on real footage (no labels), recall of missed reactions, other games/streamers/languages.
 * Timing: 13-23 s per 300 s of video on this laptop CPU path (voice + facecam + frame evidence); memory/VRAM not measured.
+
+## REAL samples, round 2 (2026-11-17 afternoon) — 9 Twitch samples, ~44 min: Kai Cenat (GTA SA, GTA IV), IShowSpeed (GTA stream), vicens (GTA V, Spanish)
+* Facecam auto-found in 9/9.
+* Weak labels: faster-whisper `base` transcripts (word timestamps). An "exclamation cluster" = >=3 reaction words or '!' within 4 s.
+  These labels are noisy (filler "bro", ASR errors) and are NOT ground truth.
+| version | picks | picks containing an exclamation | exclamation clusters caught |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| audio + facecam only | 20 | 15 (75%) | 5/33 (15%) |
+| + transcript reaction words | 23 | 17 (74%) | 7/33 (21%) |
+* The second row is partly CIRCULAR (the new signal reads the same transcript the labels come from). The honest recall figure is the first row.
+* Reading: picks are mostly real reactions; RECALL IS LOW. Most missed clusters had no agreeing facecam/voice signal, and the
+  two-signal rule (required by the amendment) rejects them. Always-loud streamers (IShowSpeed) rarely stand out acoustically.
+* Mouth-movement check (game dialogue vs streamer): ran on every voice-led pick, demoted none. Not validated on a real
+  game-dialogue false positive.
+* Kai Cenat 04:49 pick (score 95): transcript "What the hell? That shit hurt... AHHHH" — a real scream at an on-screen event.
